From: Kevin Finisterre <kf@digitalmunition.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hashtable: zero the whole table, not a pointer's size per entry

hashtable_init() cleared sizeof(callsign_hashtable), a pointer (4 bytes on the radio), for each of the
table's 16-byte entries: three quarters of it began as whatever the heap held, entries that a lookup
could take for a stored callsign and copy out without its terminating NUL.

--- a/ft8/hashtable.c
+++ b/ft8/hashtable.c
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
     callsign_hashtable_size = 0;
     callsign_hashtable_max_size = hashtable_max_size;
     callsign_hashtable = malloc(sizeof(*callsign_hashtable) * callsign_hashtable_max_size);
-    memset(callsign_hashtable, 0, sizeof(callsign_hashtable) * callsign_hashtable_max_size);
+    memset(callsign_hashtable, 0, sizeof(*callsign_hashtable) * callsign_hashtable_max_size);
 }
 
 void hashtable_delete()
